# Data Repository -- IEEE Transactions on Reliability
## Manuscript TR-2026-712

**Title:** Reliability-Constrained Available Transfer Capability Assessment
using Deep Neural Network Surrogate: Real Renewable Energy Uncertainty
and Carbon Budget Constraint

**Authors:** Kingsuk Majumdar (BCREC, Durgapur), Sohini Ghosh (BCREC),
Nishant Kumar (IIT Jodhpur)

**DOI:** https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19753213

---

## Repository Contents

This repository provides the data, pre-trained model weights, simulation
results, and validation figures that support the findings of the manuscript.
Simulation pipeline scripts are available from the corresponding author
upon reasonable request (kingsuk.majumdar@bcrec.ac.in).

---

## 1. Pre-trained DNN Surrogate Model Weights

These `.pt` files can be loaded directly in PyTorch (>=2.0) without
retraining to reproduce all DNN surrogate predictions in the paper.

| File | System | n\_in | Architecture | R² | MAE (PU) |
|------|--------|-------|-------------|-----|---------|
| `surrogate_case30.pt` | IEEE 30-bus | 80 | [256,512,256,128] | 0.9975 | 0.0037 |
| `surrogate_case118.pt` | IEEE 118-bus | 324 | [256,512,256,128] | 0.9675 | 0.0239 |
| `surrogate_nrpg246.pt` | NRPG 246-bus | 554 | [512,1024,512,256] | 0.9999 | 0.000270 |

**How to load (Python):**
```python
import torch
ck = torch.load('surrogate_case30.pt', map_location='cpu',
                weights_only=False)
# Keys: n_in, state_dict, y_mean, y_std, hidden
# y_mean=0.6484, y_std=0.1003 for case30
```

---

## 2. Original Experiment Results (30-trial CC-OSHO)

These files contain the full 30-trial reliability-constrained results
reported in Tables VI, VII, X, XI, XII, XIII of the manuscript.

| File | Contents | Manuscript table |
|------|----------|-----------------|
| `S4_full_results.json` | E[ATC], VaR90, CE, Friedman ranks -- IEEE 30-bus and 118-bus | Tab. VI, VII, X, XI |
| `S6_nrpg246_results.json` | E[ATC], VaR90 -- NRPG 246-bus (30 trials) | Tab. XII, XIII |
| `S6c_results.json` | Carbon results -- NRPG 246-bus | Tab. XII |
| `S2_baseline_results.json` | Deterministic ATC baseline (5 trials) | Tab. V |
| `S3_cc_fitness_results.json` | Stochastic fitness evaluation results | -- |

---

## 3. DNN Surrogate Validation (Tab. I of manuscript)

| File | Contents |
|------|----------|
| `S07_data02_dnn_validation_summary.csv` | R², RMSE, MAE on held-out test sets (n=1500/1000) |

**Key values (Tab. I):**

| System | n\_test | R² | RMSE (PU) | MAE (PU) |
|--------|---------|-----|-----------|---------|
| IEEE 30-bus | 1500 | 0.9975 | 0.0049 | 0.0037 |
| IEEE 118-bus | 1500 | 0.9675 | 0.0367 | 0.0239 |
| NRPG 246-bus | 1000 | 0.9999 | 0.000270 | 0.000270 |

**Figures:**
- `S07_fig01_error_histogram_case30.png` -- Error histogram, IEEE 30-bus
- `S07_fig02_error_histogram_case118.png` -- Error histogram, IEEE 118-bus
- `S07_fig04_residual_scatter.png` -- Residual scatter, both IEEE systems

---

## 4. Surrogate Model Comparison (Tab. II of manuscript)

| File | Contents |
|------|----------|
| `S11_data02_model_comparison.csv` | R², RMSE, MAE for DNN vs Linear Regression vs Random Forest |

**Key finding:** DNN achieves 41--48% lower MAE than LR and RF on
IEEE 118-bus; on IEEE 30-bus the 80 engineered features linearise the
ATC mapping so LR achieves R²=0.9999.

**Figures:**
- `S11_fig01_model_comparison_bar.png`
- `S11_fig02_scatter_comparison.png`
- `S11_fig03_error_distribution.png`

---

## 5. Out-of-Sample Validation (Tab. VIII of manuscript)

| File | Contents |
|------|----------|
| `S08_data02_oos_summary.csv` | OOS E[ATC], VaR90, bias for all 5 algorithms x 3 systems |

**Key finding:** Maximum OOS bias = +2.06% (GWO, IEEE 118-bus).
All biases positive -- in-sample results are conservative, not optimistic.

**Figures:**
- `S08_fig01_oos_eatc_case30.png`
- `S08_fig02_oos_eatc_case118.png`
- `S08_fig03_oos_eatc_nrpg.png`

---

## 6. Carbon Budget Sensitivity (Tab. IX of manuscript)

| File | Contents |
|------|----------|
| `S09_data02_carbon_sensitivity.csv` | E[ATC], CE achieved, binding rate for 7 CE budget levels |

**Key finding:** Physical minimum CE ~215 kg/h. Constraint binding
at 90--100% rate only when budget >= 120% of moderate baseline.

**Figures:**
- `S09_fig01_atc_ce_tradeoff.png`
- `S09_fig02_var90_ce_tradeoff.png`
- `S09_fig03_binding_analysis.png`

---

## 7. N-1 Contingency Off-Deployment Study

| File | Contents |
|------|----------|
| `S10_data02_n1_summary.csv` | MAE per contingency (34 lines + 7 trafos), IEEE 30-bus |

**Key finding:** Under non-critical N-1 line outages, MAE increases
by 1.2x (0.153 to 0.180 PU). Monitored trafo outage: MAE = 0.642 PU
(expected failure -- corridor removed).

**Figures:**
- `S10_fig01_error_by_contingency.png`
- `S10_fig02_error_distribution.png`
- `S10_fig03_normal_vs_n1.png`

---

